  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What you have",
      "items": [
        "A React 19 + Vite frontend and Spring Boot REST backend.",
        "The current /api \u2192 localhost:8080 route is Vite development configuration; the packaged app needs an explicit API base URL.",
        "compose.yaml starts PostgreSQL only. No Tauri/Electron wrapper or Windows/Linux installer was found."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Desktop recommendation",
      "items": [
        "Start with Tauri v2: reuse the existing React UI and package the built frontend in a native window.",
        "Keep Spring + PostgreSQL as a separately deployed service for the first release; a desktop shell alone does not make the app offline or local-first.",
        "Create Windows and Linux builds in CI/on each target OS. Choose MSI or NSIS for Windows; select Linux packages based on your supported distros."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Fix before shipping device control",
      "items": [
        "TaskManagerService uses ProcessHandle inside the Spring host JVM. A remote backend therefore sees/controls server processes, not the user's PC.",
        "The existing Linux Rust/Python shields poll the API and can terminate name-matched processes; both default auto-kill on. Do not simply package them as a desktop feature.",
        "Move local-device operations behind typed, least-privilege native commands; begin read-only, require explicit user policy/consent, and verify outcomes. Do not expose arbitrary shell execution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Worktree snapshot at diagram creation",
      "items": [
